    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="9">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 9</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="9" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gemeta ⁊ gewihta rihte man georne ⁊ ælces unrihtes heonan forð geswíce.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="9" corresp="#wit-a">And gemétta ⁊ gewyhta rihta man georne ⁊ ælces unrihtes heonan forð geswicæ.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="9" corresp="#wit-q">Mensurę et pondera iustificentur, et omnis iniusticia deinceps opprimatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="9" corresp="#wit-b">Geméta ⁊ gewihta rihte man georne ⁊ ælces unrihtes [heonan forð] geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gemeta and gewihta rihte man georne and ælces unrihtes heonon forð geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">Measures and weights shall be diligently corrected, and an end put to all unjust practices.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And weights and measures are to be assiduously made right, and all unlawful practices abolished henceforth.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und Maasse und Gewichte mache man genau richtig und lasse hinfort von jedem Unrecht ab.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let measures and weights be carefully corrected, and let every injustice cease henceforth.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="315"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_32-2">VI Atr 32.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">VI Atr. 32, 2</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:WlArtRetr_7">Wl art retr 7</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 32.2.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">heonon forð: omitted B</note>
      </div>
    </body>
